    "engine": "jupyter",
    "markdown": "---\ngd-head-tags:\n  - >-\n    `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">[{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"SoftwareSourceCode\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\", \"description\":\n    \"High-performance graph analysis library\", \"codeRepository\":\n    \"https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase\", \"license\":\n    \"https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT\", \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"documentation\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"programmingLanguage\": {\"@type\":\n    \"ComputerLanguage\", \"name\": \"Python\"}}, {\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\", \"name\": \"Graph.bfs_successors - EdgeCase\", \"isPartOf\":\n    {\"@type\": \"WebSite\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\"}, \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase/reference/Graph.bfs_successors.html\"}]</script>`{=html}\nopen-graph:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.bfs_successors()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Map every node of a breadth-first search tree to its children.\ntwitter-card:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.bfs_successors()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Map every node of a breadth-first search tree to its children.\ntitle: >-\n  [Graph.bfs_successors()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n  .doc-label-method}\nbody-classes: doc-api-page doc-py-api-page\nshift-heading-level-by: 0\nbread-crumbs: false\ntoc-depth: 3\ndescription-meta: Map every node of a breadth-first search tree to its children.\npage-navigation: false\nhtml-table-processing: none\n---\n\n::: {.doc-subject}\n\nMap every node of a breadth-first search tree to its children.\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-usage-source}\nUsage\n\n[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase/blob/main/python/edgecase/graph.py#L64223-L64303){target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"}\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-signature .doc-function}\n```pythonsignature\nGraph.bfs_successors(\n    source,\n    depth_limit=None,\n    mode=\"out\",\n)\n```\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-text}\n\n![BFS successors](../assets/graphs/bfs-successors.light.svg){.lightbox fig-alt=\"The same four-node tree searched breadth-first from A (outlined). Each accent arrow points from a parent to a child it discovered, and numbered badges give the discovery order. The card maps A to its children B and C, and C to D; the leaves B and D are not keys.\" width=\"100%\"}\n\nThe reverse view of `bfs_predecessors()`: for each node of the breadth-first search tree\nfrom `source` that has children, the list of nodes discovered from it. It shows how the\nsearch fans out, level by level, such as who first heard a rumor from whom.\n:::\n\n## Parameters {.doc-parameters}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code>[source]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Union[int, str]]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   The start node, as an ID or label.\n\n<code>[depth_limit]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [int | None]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Optional maximum depth.\n\n<code>[mode]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [str]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [[&quot;out&quot;]{.st}]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Edge direction to follow on directed graphs: `\"out\"` (default), `\"in\"` or `\"all\"`.\n:::\n\n## Returns {.doc-returns}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [dict[int, list[int]]]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   Parent node ID to the list of its children, in discovery order (leaves are not keys,\n    except the source, which maps to an empty list when it has no children).\n:::\n\n## Raises {.doc-raises}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [ValueError]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   If the source does not exist or `mode` is invalid.\n:::\n\n## Technical Notes {.doc-technical-notes}\n\nGrouped from the tree edges of `bfs_edges()`. Matches NetworkX's `bfs_successors`.\n\n## See Also {.doc-see-also}\n\n[](`~bfs_predecessors`) \n\n:   The same tree, from each node to the node it was reached from.\n\n[](`~dfs_successors`) \n\n:   The successors from a depth-first search.\n\n## Examples {.doc-examples}\n\nEach node maps to the nodes the search reached from it:\n\n::: {#cd70eefe .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport edgecase as ec\n\ngraph = ec.Graph.from_edges([(\"A\", \"B\"), (\"A\", \"C\"), (\"C\", \"D\")])\n\nlabel = graph.get_label_from_id\nnext_nodes = graph.bfs_successors(\"A\")\n{label(p): [label(c) for c in cs] for p, cs in next_nodes.items()}\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}\n```\n{'A': ['B', 'C'], 'C': ['D']}\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n### What a course opens up\n\n`courses()` links each course of a made-up degree program to the courses that require it.\nSearching from CS101, each course maps to the courses first reached from it, giving the\nfewest steps from CS101 to each course that needs it:\n\n::: {#2072a01f .cell execution_count=2}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\ncourses = ec.courses()\nopens = courses.bfs_successors(\"CS101\")\n\nlabel = courses.get_label_from_id\n{label(p): [label(c) for c in cs] for p, cs in opens.items()}\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=2}\n```\n{'CS101': ['CS102', 'CS201'],\n 'CS102': ['CS210', 'CS220', 'CS250'],\n 'CS201': ['CS360'],\n 'CS210': ['CS310', 'CS320'],\n 'CS250': ['CS350'],\n 'CS360': ['CS460'],\n 'CS310': ['CS410']}\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n::: {#29c3a93f .cell execution_count=3}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nsteps = [(p, c) for p, cs in opens.items() for c in cs]\ncourses.plot(highlight=steps, label_by=\"label\", seed=2)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=3}\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"ec-theme\" style=\"display:contents\"><style class=\"ec-theme-vars\">:where(.ec-theme){--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;